-- Riverglades (zone 16591): put our spawns on the ground. Their heights were guessed when the zone's data came in (2026_11_08_96,
-- 2026_11_10_73, 2026_11_11_74 and later), so some NPCs stood under the ground or in the air (GitHub issue #20, 2026-11-21, with
-- screenshots). 2026_11_12_33 only moved the 57 creatures that could not walk. The new heights come from the server's own map 0 navmesh
-- (mmap_probe on the dev realm, 2026-11-21, 21 probes per spawn from 80 yd below to 80 yd above): the walkable point straight above
-- or below the old spot, nearest to the old height. Only spawns more than 2 yd off it, and only our own data (Forever creature
-- entries 250000+, gameobject entries 600000+, our guids 47000000+); Blizzard-era spawns in the box are not touched. Spawns under the
-- sea surface, and the swimmers 257916/260968 in the inland lakes, are water dwellers and stay where they are.
-- Moves over 20 yd are held for a look in game (may stand on a cliff or roof the navmesh does not cover).
-- INFERRED: spawns over water go onto the water surface. Each row checks guid and entry. Safe to run again.

